  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/17922d1ffef1dcd8bc798c8ffb8fe113a7e2e57cacc234641c84f59bbbcf6bbd.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OC}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & =m∠BOC+m∠COD \\\\  & ={52}^{∘}+{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ={102}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
